					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2174701#post-4845700</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2174701/the-blackbird-and-the-falcon#post-4845700</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 15 Dec 2020 21:02:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DarkStuff</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1581620</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Absolutely stellar conclusion to this whole thing. Anderson is such a little prick and I like him a lot. I would like to say that I don't see the Foundation as <em>good guys</em> throughout all of this. You paint very sympathetic characters on both sides, up to and including Anderson himself, and Conwell has very real concerns about the methods they are using to achieve their goals. I was definitely not solely rooting for the foundation here, let us just say that.</p> <p>Anderson's final play is fantastic. The action scenes were thrilling. The use of multiple formats to show different perspectives was well-done. Everything was well-paced. Felt epic, in the non-slang use of that word. A mere +1 feels wrong, but it and a comment are all I can give.</p> <p>I'll say it again: stellar.</p> <p>(RIP Jacob, may he be Sakerized)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2174701#post-4838180</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2174701/the-blackbird-and-the-falcon#post-4838180</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 06 Dec 2020 21:31:14 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Gaffsey</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6590029</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Man, way to blow a hole in my pet theory<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-72682-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>. Still, a fantastic piece from start to finish. It's a bit hard to enjoy as a definitive last word on Anderson unless the remaining 40% of the canon is going to be denouement after denouement after denouement.</p> <p>Wasn't really-really feeling the Conwell bits, as they were merely good, as opposed to great, but I'll let it slide.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-72682-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Captive!Anderson and Saker!Anderson would form divergent views and ultimately the clash between them would revolve around some meaningful philosophical difference, with Captive!Anderson having to face what he'd done to Phineas, his family, etc. while Saker!Anderson could just giving out gifts as &quot;Get Out Of Jail Free&quot; cards.</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
