				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2174701#post-2773002</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2174701/the-blackbird-and-the-falcon#post-2773002</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 22 Mar 2017 10:15:13 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>TBlackburn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1496792</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This was a very very nice read, and a fine 'end' to the tales. Even if it's an open ending.</p> <p>I just feel a little ambivalent about Andersons final play.</p> <p>On the one hand it makes sense for someone as he's been portrayed to have backup plans within backup plans on hand to get himself that final win over Merlot in some form of Xanatos Gambit and turn the taste of her victory into ashes in her mouth in the end&#8230;</p> <p>On the other hand, I really wanted her to have that victory at last.</p> <p>The numerous references to Moby Dick did kindof make it clear that she wasn't going to get it though. Thankfully it's less disastrous in the end than it could have been.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
